WEBVTT

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:39.189
A hush comes over the crowd.

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:43.860
The only sound is Bender calling
everyone else a jerk as he swings!

00:00:44.695 --> 00:00:47.406
Aw, he slices into the water!

00:00:47.489 --> 00:00:49.324
Oh, man!

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:53.996
Boy, I'll tell you, man...

00:00:56.949 --> 00:00:58.283
Bad news, everyone.

00:00:58.367 --> 00:01:01.203
You're not good enough
to go on your next mission.

00:01:01.286 --> 00:01:03.538
- Hooray!
- Not good enough!

00:01:03.622 --> 00:01:04.873
Why? Says who?

00:01:04.957 --> 00:01:07.000
Because. And says me.

00:01:07.084 --> 00:01:11.004
It's an extremely dangerous mission
that killed my last crew,

00:01:11.088 --> 00:01:12.798
and you're not nearly as good as them.

00:01:12.881 --> 00:01:13.924
Whoo-hoo!

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:15.509
We live to suck another day.

00:01:18.637 --> 00:01:19.888
Oh!

00:01:19.972 --> 00:01:24.101
We are just as good as any of those
other crews you sent to their deaths.

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:25.352
What's the mission?

00:01:25.435 --> 00:01:26.728
Collecting honey.

00:01:26.812 --> 00:01:27.980
Ordinary honey.

00:01:28.063 --> 00:01:29.606
That doesn't sound so dangerous.

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:31.692
This is no ordinary honey.

00:01:31.775 --> 00:01:34.278
It's produced by vicious space bees.

00:01:34.361 --> 00:01:38.824
A single sting of their hideous neurotoxin
can cause instant death.

00:01:38.907 --> 00:01:40.534
And that's if you're not allergic.

00:01:40.617 --> 00:01:43.620
You don't want to know what happens then.
No, no, no, God no.

00:01:43.704 --> 00:01:46.540
Your insides will boil
out of your eye sockets

00:01:46.623 --> 00:01:48.458
like a science fair volcano.

00:01:48.542 --> 00:01:50.168
I didn't want to know.

00:01:51.628 --> 00:01:54.464
These bees are larger than most Buicks.

00:01:54.548 --> 00:01:55.841
And twice as ugly.

00:01:55.924 --> 00:01:57.843
Larger than an American sedan?

00:01:57.926 --> 00:01:59.886
Whoo, how big is the honeycomb?

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:02.556
Honeycomb's big... Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:02.639 --> 00:02:03.765
It's not small?

00:02:03.849 --> 00:02:05.100
No, no, no.

00:02:05.183 --> 00:02:09.354
It'll take more than deadly, deadly bees
to keep us from doing our job.

00:02:09.438 --> 00:02:10.564
Come on, boys.

00:02:10.647 --> 00:02:11.940
But, Leela, we're no good.

00:02:12.024 --> 00:02:16.361
Listen, I'm scared, too, but I'm more
scared of disappointing myself.

00:02:16.445 --> 00:02:18.030
I'm not scared of that at all.

00:02:41.053 --> 00:02:43.388
Now, bees communicate by dancing.

00:02:43.472 --> 00:02:44.473
Like my parents.

00:02:44.556 --> 00:02:46.224
Oh, wait, that was hitting.

00:02:46.308 --> 00:02:49.102
So this language cartridge
will let you distract them.

00:02:49.186 --> 00:02:50.270
Ah, good.

00:02:50.354 --> 00:02:54.107
I often have thoughts and feelings
that can only be expressed through dance.

00:03:07.454 --> 00:03:09.414
Bender, quick, waggle something.

00:03:09.498 --> 00:03:10.582
Uh...

00:03:22.052 --> 00:03:23.261
Leela, let's turn back.

00:03:23.345 --> 00:03:25.555
There's absolutely no shame
in wussing out.

00:03:25.639 --> 00:03:27.683
Relax. Everything will be fine.

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:31.270
Oh, my God.

00:03:31.353 --> 00:03:33.063
The old Planet Express ship.

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:34.648
There's the black box.

00:03:36.191 --> 00:03:38.485
Captain,
the beeshave us surrounded!

00:03:38.568 --> 00:03:39.861
Oh, the professor was right.

00:03:39.945 --> 00:03:41.738
We're not as good as his old crew.

00:03:41.822 --> 00:03:43.365
Well, I aim to prove him wrong.

00:03:43.448 --> 00:03:45.909
It'll take more than a few
deadly, deadly bees to...

00:03:45.993 --> 00:03:47.577
Oh, Lord!

00:03:49.746 --> 00:03:51.540
Uh, I couldn't make that out.

00:03:51.623 --> 00:03:53.292
Too much static.

00:04:03.719 --> 00:04:05.012
Ew.

00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:13.437
We found it! The honeycomb hideout.

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:19.985
Hey, what's this goo?

00:04:20.068 --> 00:04:21.069
Royal jelly.

00:04:21.153 --> 00:04:22.362
They feed it to the queen.

00:04:22.446 --> 00:04:24.740
Bees make honey and jelly?

00:04:24.823 --> 00:04:27.576
Huh, how come nothing humans
make tastes good?

00:04:31.455 --> 00:04:34.583
Help! I can't swim in jelly,
as far as I know!

00:04:37.044 --> 00:04:38.128
Look.

00:04:39.296 --> 00:04:41.423
It's a baby queen.

00:04:41.548 --> 00:04:44.092
Aw, she's so cute.

00:04:44.176 --> 00:04:48.096
You adorable wittle,
itty-bitty, fuzzy-wuzzy...

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:50.182
Leela, stop bonding and let's go.

00:04:50.265 --> 00:04:51.934
I got jelly in my underpants.

00:04:52.017 --> 00:04:53.685
I'm taking this bee with us.

00:04:53.769 --> 00:04:57.272
With a queen, we can build a hive
and make more honey ourselves.

00:04:57.356 --> 00:04:59.900
Let me just pack her a lunch and we'll go.

00:04:59.983 --> 00:05:01.318
Pick up the pace, lady.

00:05:06.281 --> 00:05:08.283
Uh, I didn't mean you're all fat.

00:05:26.385 --> 00:05:29.638
This is where we distinguish ourselves
from the last crew.

00:05:29.721 --> 00:05:32.099
Activate emergency
high-speed self-contained

00:05:32.182 --> 00:05:34.059
escape pack crisis response units.

00:05:34.142 --> 00:05:35.477
Quick.

00:05:47.531 --> 00:05:48.949
Ow! Ow!

00:06:00.836 --> 00:06:02.671
Good luck, Bender.

00:06:17.269 --> 00:06:18.687
I'm back, baby!

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:30.032
We made it! We're alive!

00:06:30.115 --> 00:06:31.491
Burn on that old crew.

00:06:31.575 --> 00:06:34.453
The only things they did better than us
were suck and die.

00:06:34.536 --> 00:06:35.996
Leela, we got lucky this time.

00:06:36.079 --> 00:06:37.581
But you should be more careful.

00:06:37.664 --> 00:06:39.374
I don't want anything to happen to you.

00:06:39.458 --> 00:06:41.710
Thanks, but I can look out for myself.

00:06:41.793 --> 00:06:44.588
Frankly, I can smell danger a mile away.

00:06:44.671 --> 00:06:45.714
Look out!

00:06:48.467 --> 00:06:50.427
If you want her,
you're going to have to go through me.

00:07:04.024 --> 00:07:05.525
You call that a wound?

00:07:05.609 --> 00:07:07.235
That's a boo-boo, tops.

00:07:07.319 --> 00:07:09.363
But thanks for trying to save me, Fry.

00:07:09.863 --> 00:07:11.114
Fry?

00:07:12.866 --> 00:07:15.619
He's... He's dead.

00:07:17.621 --> 00:07:23.251
Oh, who will make Bender waffles
just the way he likes them now?

00:07:45.607 --> 00:07:47.651
It was all my fault.

00:07:47.734 --> 00:07:49.569
He died because of me.

00:07:49.653 --> 00:07:53.282
No, no, no.

00:07:53.365 --> 00:07:55.701
I'm lying to make her feel better.

00:08:00.247 --> 00:08:03.417
Husband, can't you go anywhere
without lighting something up?

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:05.877
It's an old Jamaican accounting tradition.

00:08:05.961 --> 00:08:07.462
We burn his time card.

00:08:07.546 --> 00:08:10.882
That way, his zombie doesn't come back
looking for his final paycheck.

00:08:11.508 --> 00:08:13.468
He looks so natural.

00:08:13.552 --> 00:08:16.930
It's funny to think he's crammed full
of sawdust and preservatives.

00:08:17.014 --> 00:08:19.683
I only wish I could
have removed the stinger.

00:08:23.103 --> 00:08:24.813
I barely knew Philip,

00:08:24.896 --> 00:08:26.898
but as a clergyman, I have no problem

00:08:26.982 --> 00:08:29.192
telling his most intimate friends
all about him.

00:08:30.986 --> 00:08:32.863
Soothe us with sweet lies.

00:08:32.946 --> 00:08:36.992
It may comfort you to know
Fry's death took only 15 seconds.

00:08:37.075 --> 00:08:42.080
Yet the pain was so intense
that it felt to him like 15 years,

00:08:42.164 --> 00:08:44.041
and it goes without saying

00:08:44.124 --> 00:08:46.627
it caused him to empty his bowels.

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:48.545
Aw!

00:08:48.629 --> 00:08:52.007
We now commend Fry's body to the ages.

00:09:01.558 --> 00:09:03.852
He's walking on sunshine now.

00:09:04.144 --> 00:09:08.440
This make me
the oldest member of my family.

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:14.112
Him do good snu-snu.

00:09:14.196 --> 00:09:15.238
Eh.

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:20.035
All those times I said, "Kill all humans,"

00:09:20.118 --> 00:09:22.746
I'd always whisper, "Except one."

00:09:22.829 --> 00:09:24.873
Fry was that one.

00:09:24.957 --> 00:09:27.834
And I never told him so.

00:09:30.212 --> 00:09:33.966
Farewell from the world of tomorrow!

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:51.233
They say a spoonful of space honey
helps ease the pain.

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:05.205
Mm, it's good.

00:10:06.623 --> 00:10:07.916
I feel funny.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:09.668
"Ha-ha" funny.

00:10:12.921 --> 00:10:13.922
Huh?

00:10:26.059 --> 00:10:27.060
Leela?

00:10:27.144 --> 00:10:28.145
Fry?

00:10:28.228 --> 00:10:29.396
I thought you were dead.

00:10:29.479 --> 00:10:30.939
Nope, I'm better than ever.

00:10:31.023 --> 00:10:32.899
Before the accident, I couldn't do this...

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:35.277
Impressive.

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:38.030
But it does sort of support
my "You are dead" theory.

00:10:38.113 --> 00:10:39.573
Then I'll prove I'm alive

00:10:39.656 --> 00:10:41.783
by telling you something
only I could know.

00:10:41.867 --> 00:10:43.910
There's a surprise for you in my locker.

00:10:43.994 --> 00:10:46.455
I got it at a Swedish novelty shop
before we left.

00:10:51.293 --> 00:10:52.878
It's too beautiful to open.

00:10:52.961 --> 00:10:54.046
Can I open it?

00:10:54.129 --> 00:10:56.506
Sure. There's just one thing
I want you to do.

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:57.591
What?

00:10:57.674 --> 00:10:58.884
I want you to wake up.

00:10:58.967 --> 00:11:00.427
Wake up? But I'm not...

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:07.517
In my dream, Fry said he hid
a gift for me in his locker.

00:11:07.601 --> 00:11:10.729
If it's true, then he must
still exist in some form.

00:11:10.812 --> 00:11:12.481
Of course he still exists...

00:11:12.564 --> 00:11:14.983
As a frozen corpse in outer space.

00:11:17.736 --> 00:11:19.655
I made myself sad.

00:11:19.738 --> 00:11:21.448
Well, here it goes.

00:11:27.829 --> 00:11:28.830
Oh...

00:11:28.914 --> 00:11:29.915
Bupkes.

00:11:32.751 --> 00:11:34.169
Well, I feel better now.

00:11:34.252 --> 00:11:37.714
Pawning all the stuff in Fry's locker
helped give me closure.

00:11:37.798 --> 00:11:40.050
Was there anything in there
that might have been a gift for me?

00:11:40.133 --> 00:11:41.301
Nope, nothing.

00:11:41.385 --> 00:11:42.386
Not at all.

00:11:42.469 --> 00:11:43.971
No way, Jose.

00:11:44.596 --> 00:11:45.597
Here it is.

00:11:46.932 --> 00:11:48.725
You took this from Fry's locker?

00:11:48.809 --> 00:11:49.893
Hey, the guy's dead.

00:11:49.977 --> 00:11:51.645
There's no law against grave robbing.

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:57.526
That proves it.

00:11:57.609 --> 00:11:59.278
Fry is alive somewhere

00:11:59.361 --> 00:12:01.446
and he's reaching me in my dreams.

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:02.572
Bull pies!

00:12:04.199 --> 00:12:06.868
Lay down here, and we'll do some tests.

00:12:06.952 --> 00:12:08.870
If Fry is out there somewhere,

00:12:08.954 --> 00:12:12.624
Leela's brain could be acting
as a five-pound Ouija board.

00:12:13.417 --> 00:12:15.127
Is this some sort of brain scanner?

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:16.461
Some sort, yes.

00:12:16.545 --> 00:12:18.755
In France, it's called a guillotine.

00:12:20.549 --> 00:12:21.633
Professor!

00:12:21.717 --> 00:12:23.719
Can't you examine my brain
without removing it?

00:12:23.802 --> 00:12:25.429
Yes, easily.

00:12:27.222 --> 00:12:30.267
Hey, what if Fry wasn't actually
dead when we buried him?

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:31.810
You know, like Julia Roberts?

00:12:31.893 --> 00:12:33.437
Well, I suppose there's a slim...

00:12:35.856 --> 00:12:37.566
I don't believe it!

00:12:37.649 --> 00:12:38.859
What is it?

00:12:38.942 --> 00:12:40.777
Is Fry alive in some
other dimension or something?

00:12:40.861 --> 00:12:43.739
No! According to this gizmometer,

00:12:43.822 --> 00:12:46.283
Fry is dead,
and nothing can bring him back.

00:12:46.366 --> 00:12:47.743
Remarkable.

00:12:47.826 --> 00:12:49.745
But my dream.

00:12:49.828 --> 00:12:52.080
Your science can't unprove that.

00:12:52.164 --> 00:12:54.458
How could I have known
the gift was in Fry's locker?

00:12:54.541 --> 00:12:55.709
Easy.

00:12:55.792 --> 00:12:57.419
He told you about it before he died

00:12:57.502 --> 00:12:59.546
and your grief-roasted mind
blocked it out.

00:12:59.921 --> 00:13:01.298
Are you saying

00:13:01.381 --> 00:13:02.799
I'm going crazy?

00:13:02.883 --> 00:13:04.051
No, no.

00:13:04.134 --> 00:13:05.302
No one's saying that,

00:13:05.385 --> 00:13:07.638
but I'm certainly thinking it loudly.

00:13:19.441 --> 00:13:22.444
Hi, Leela. I'm just going to keep talking
even if you can't hear me.

00:13:22.527 --> 00:13:24.321
Blah, blah, blah...

00:13:24.404 --> 00:13:26.114
Shut up, I can hear you.

00:13:26.198 --> 00:13:27.991
The professor says you're just a dream.

00:13:28.075 --> 00:13:29.701
Oh, yeah?

00:13:30.702 --> 00:13:33.497
Could a dream take you dancing
in a Venusian garden?

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:37.876
Well, yes, technically,
but it's still very sweet of you.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:39.753
Then what if we shared
a midnight sleigh ride

00:13:39.836 --> 00:13:42.047
across the ice fields of Hyperion?

00:13:51.264 --> 00:13:53.350
Oh, Fry, you must be alive.

00:13:53.433 --> 00:13:55.310
I've never been treated so romantically

00:13:55.394 --> 00:13:57.229
by my own imagination before.

00:13:57.312 --> 00:13:59.064
Here, take my jacket.

00:13:59.147 --> 00:14:00.440
You look a little cold.

00:14:01.108 --> 00:14:02.192
Thank you.

00:14:02.276 --> 00:14:03.986
It's all so beautiful.

00:14:04.069 --> 00:14:07.114
I forgot how many hundreds of degrees
below zero it must be.

00:14:07.197 --> 00:14:09.950
I just wish I could convince
the others you're alive.

00:14:10.033 --> 00:14:12.286
You can. All you have to do is wake up.

00:14:12.369 --> 00:14:14.204
No, no, don't say that!

00:14:14.288 --> 00:14:15.289
This is real!

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:18.125
Not another dream!

00:14:20.669 --> 00:14:21.795
Fry's jacket!

00:14:21.878 --> 00:14:23.588
The one he was buried in.

00:14:23.672 --> 00:14:25.215
My dream was real.

00:14:25.299 --> 00:14:26.800
He's alive!

00:14:27.968 --> 00:14:31.054
Quit your bragging.
My boyfriend's alive, too.

00:14:31.138 --> 00:14:33.557
Uh, not anymore.

00:14:42.858 --> 00:14:44.067
That's better.

00:14:47.946 --> 00:14:50.032
Fry's alive! I have proof!

00:14:50.115 --> 00:14:51.783
- What?
- You do not.

00:14:51.867 --> 00:14:53.994
I'm from Jamaica, the "Show Me" island.

00:14:54.077 --> 00:14:56.246
So show me you blowing it out your fanny.

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:58.582
But he gave me his jacket. Look.

00:14:59.875 --> 00:15:01.627
That's not Fry's jacket.

00:15:01.710 --> 00:15:03.337
Fry's jacket is red.

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:04.504
That's your jacket,

00:15:04.588 --> 00:15:06.882
an off-the-rack lime-green affair.

00:15:06.965 --> 00:15:08.008
But Fry...

00:15:08.091 --> 00:15:09.217
His jacket...

00:15:09.301 --> 00:15:11.428
And when I woke up, it was on me.

00:15:11.511 --> 00:15:13.805
You're under a lot of guilt stress, Leela.

00:15:13.889 --> 00:15:15.140
Here, work it out.

00:15:15.223 --> 00:15:18.393
I am not under stress, damn it!

00:15:18.477 --> 00:15:20.938
Everything's going to be all right, Leela.

00:15:21.021 --> 00:15:22.022
What?

00:15:22.105 --> 00:15:24.274
I said
everything's going to be all right.

00:15:24.358 --> 00:15:27.194
Uh... Maybe I am freaking out a little.

00:15:27.277 --> 00:15:29.947
A little? You're screwier
than my Aunt Rita.

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:31.198
And she's a screw.

00:15:31.281 --> 00:15:32.783
I need to calm down.

00:15:32.866 --> 00:15:34.826
I better take some more
of that space honey.

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:36.787
You've been taking space honey?

00:15:36.870 --> 00:15:39.373
Be careful, you purple-haired imbecile.

00:15:39.456 --> 00:15:41.583
One spoonful calms you down.

00:15:41.667 --> 00:15:43.794
Two spoonfuls helps you sleep.

00:15:43.877 --> 00:15:47.172
But three spoonfuls
and you'll go into a sleep so deep

00:15:47.255 --> 00:15:48.382
you'll never wake up!

00:15:48.465 --> 00:15:49.466
Never!

00:15:49.549 --> 00:15:50.634
Never!

00:15:50.717 --> 00:15:51.885
Never!

00:15:55.138 --> 00:15:57.599
One spoonful to calm me down.

00:16:02.062 --> 00:16:04.940
Okay, I got a pretty good calm going.

00:16:05.649 --> 00:16:07.818
Two spoonfuls to help me sleep.

00:16:10.487 --> 00:16:12.281
Uh-oh... Still awake.

00:16:12.364 --> 00:16:14.574
I guess one more spoonful couldn't hurt.

00:16:14.658 --> 00:16:16.034
Ugh!

00:16:16.702 --> 00:16:18.870
Oh, my gosh! I better get a sponge.

00:16:22.749 --> 00:16:23.959
Fry?

00:16:24.042 --> 00:16:25.127
Is that you?

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:26.753
I don't need a sponge.

00:16:28.338 --> 00:16:30.257
Why am I sticky and naked?

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:31.800
Did I miss something fun?

00:16:33.885 --> 00:16:35.387
Incredible.

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:37.639
According to the gizmometer,

00:16:37.723 --> 00:16:39.850
Fry touched the royal jelly
in the space hive,

00:16:39.933 --> 00:16:43.186
leaving an imprint
of his DNA and brain waves.

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:45.647
Then, when it spilled on the couch,

00:16:45.731 --> 00:16:48.692
it recombined with
trace amounts of Fry's hair and skin...

00:16:48.775 --> 00:16:50.027
And blood.

00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:51.653
Don't forget about Fry's blood.

00:16:51.737 --> 00:16:53.196
Yes, Bender, thank you.

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:56.533
In short, the various fluids
Fry left in the couch

00:16:56.617 --> 00:17:00.203
caused the royal jelly
to regenerate his entire being.

00:17:00.287 --> 00:17:02.247
- Neat.
- This is great.

00:17:02.331 --> 00:17:05.292
My buddy's alive
and his credit cards are valid again.

00:17:05.375 --> 00:17:06.585
Let's go get hammered!

00:17:08.378 --> 00:17:09.463
I should warn you,

00:17:09.546 --> 00:17:11.048
I'm a mean drunk.

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:15.302
- Fry, I'm so glad I didn't kill you.
- Me, too.

00:17:15.385 --> 00:17:18.388
Feeling responsible for your death
was driving me mad,

00:17:18.472 --> 00:17:20.307
but now everything is all right.

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:21.892
Uh, not everything.

00:17:21.975 --> 00:17:23.810
What? What do you mean?

00:17:23.894 --> 00:17:25.145
You have to wake up.

00:17:25.228 --> 00:17:26.480
Wake up?

00:17:26.563 --> 00:17:29.274
Oh, no... No! It can't be!

00:17:31.735 --> 00:17:32.861
Poo.

00:17:33.195 --> 00:17:34.446
I'm cracking up.

00:17:34.529 --> 00:17:36.949
In my dreams,
I'm happy because Fry is alive,

00:17:37.032 --> 00:17:39.660
but when I'm awake,
my mind plays tricks on me.

00:17:39.743 --> 00:17:41.578
Aw, take it easy, Leela.

00:17:41.662 --> 00:17:44.414
In every life, we have some trouble.

00:17:44.498 --> 00:17:46.959
But when you worry, you make it double.

00:17:47.042 --> 00:17:48.627
Don't worry

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:50.087
Be happy

00:17:51.546 --> 00:17:54.299
The landlord say your rent is late

00:17:54.383 --> 00:17:56.802
He may have to litigate

00:17:56.885 --> 00:17:59.763
But don't worry

00:17:59.846 --> 00:18:01.890
- Be...
- Happy

00:18:03.558 --> 00:18:06.561
Ain't got no cash
Ain't got no style

00:18:06.645 --> 00:18:08.730
Ladies vomit when I smile

00:18:08.814 --> 00:18:10.107
But does Zoidberg worry?

00:18:10.190 --> 00:18:12.150
Feh! You wish.

00:18:12.234 --> 00:18:13.944
- Be...
- Happy

00:18:14.027 --> 00:18:16.113
Don't worry now, Amy

00:18:16.196 --> 00:18:18.949
Okay, I'm happy

00:18:19.032 --> 00:18:20.951
Takes us home, Bender!

00:18:21.034 --> 00:18:22.619
Don't worry

00:18:23.996 --> 00:18:25.706
- Be...
- Happy.

00:18:30.752 --> 00:18:32.629
Uh... Were you just singing?

00:18:32.713 --> 00:18:34.631
No, I was telling you not to worry.

00:18:34.715 --> 00:18:36.300
I'm not allowed to sing.

00:18:36.383 --> 00:18:37.426
Court order.

00:18:42.306 --> 00:18:45.642
I'll find Fry's coffin, get his corpse
and keep it under my mattress

00:18:45.726 --> 00:18:47.519
to remind me that he's really dead.

00:18:47.603 --> 00:18:49.021
That'll prove I'm not insane.

00:19:01.116 --> 00:19:04.119
Okay, it's just an ordinary coffin

00:19:04.202 --> 00:19:07.581
containing my ordinary dead friend
who I killed.

00:19:22.929 --> 00:19:24.014
What happened?

00:19:24.097 --> 00:19:25.474
Why am I in my apartment?

00:19:25.557 --> 00:19:27.351
You killed Fry!

00:19:27.434 --> 00:19:30.187
You killed Fry! You killed Fry!

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:31.271
Stop it!

00:19:31.355 --> 00:19:32.606
- Stop it!
- You killed Fry.

00:19:34.107 --> 00:19:35.400
You killed Fry.

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:40.864
Okay, I'm insane,

00:19:40.948 --> 00:19:42.908
but I'm still sane enough to know it.

00:19:43.867 --> 00:19:47.746
The only time I feel all right
is in my dreams, with you.

00:19:48.538 --> 00:19:52.876
Three spoonfuls, then I can dream forever.

00:19:55.504 --> 00:19:56.880
One.

00:19:59.424 --> 00:20:00.592
Two.

00:20:01.259 --> 00:20:02.427
Here goes.

00:20:02.678 --> 00:20:04.554
Goodbye, waking world.

00:20:06.848 --> 00:20:08.183
Leela, no!

00:20:08.976 --> 00:20:11.270
Listen to me. You don't want to lie in bed
like a vegetable

00:20:11.353 --> 00:20:12.896
and do nothing the rest of your life.

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:14.022
I've tried it.

00:20:14.106 --> 00:20:15.190
Bedsores hurt!

00:20:15.274 --> 00:20:17.109
Then what am I supposed to do?

00:20:17.192 --> 00:20:18.902
- Fight it!
- I can't!

00:20:18.986 --> 00:20:21.613
You can! The Leela I know
doesn't give up this easily.

00:20:22.155 --> 00:20:24.533
Okay, I'll try.

00:20:27.452 --> 00:20:28.787
Go away!

00:20:33.667 --> 00:20:35.669
I don't know if you can hear me, Leela,

00:20:35.752 --> 00:20:38.130
but there's something I want to tell you.

00:20:38.213 --> 00:20:39.298
I love you.

00:20:39.381 --> 00:20:40.674
I'm so scared, Fry.

00:20:40.757 --> 00:20:42.467
I don't know what to do.

00:20:42.551 --> 00:20:44.136
Just wake up, Leela.

00:20:44.219 --> 00:20:45.846
Please, just wake up.

00:20:45.929 --> 00:20:48.348
I don't understand what you mean.

00:20:48.432 --> 00:20:50.809
Just wake up.

00:20:50.892 --> 00:20:53.687
Please. Just wake up, Leela.

00:20:57.399 --> 00:20:59.776
Fry... You're alive.

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:01.403
Leela, you're awake!

00:21:01.486 --> 00:21:02.779
Of course I'm awake.

00:21:02.863 --> 00:21:04.781
You wouldn't stop waking me.

00:21:04.865 --> 00:21:06.908
- Where am I?
- In the hospital.

00:21:06.992 --> 00:21:09.244
The ambulance took you here
right after the bee stung you.

00:21:09.328 --> 00:21:12.080
But the bee stung you.
It barely touched me.

00:21:12.956 --> 00:21:15.500
The stinger went right through me
and you got all the poison.

00:21:15.584 --> 00:21:18.211
My new spleen came from a guy
who liked to motorcycle.

00:21:18.295 --> 00:21:20.297
Vroom-vroom!

00:21:21.048 --> 00:21:23.759
Sweet three-toed sloth of ice planet Hoth!

00:21:23.842 --> 00:21:24.968
She's awake!

00:21:26.345 --> 00:21:28.555
You were in the best coma I've ever seen.

00:21:28.639 --> 00:21:30.766
The doctors said you'd never wake up.

00:21:30.849 --> 00:21:33.018
Really? How long was I out?

00:21:33.101 --> 00:21:34.102
Two weeks.

00:21:34.186 --> 00:21:36.396
Fry never left your side for a minute.

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:37.773
And he talked nonstop.

00:21:37.856 --> 00:21:39.566
Like a parrot of the sea, he was.

00:21:39.942 --> 00:21:42.402
I thought maybe
if you heard a familiar voice

00:21:42.486 --> 00:21:44.363
it might help keep your mind together,

00:21:44.446 --> 00:21:46.949
but who knows if it really got through.

00:21:47.032 --> 00:21:48.533
It got through, Fry.

00:21:49.534 --> 00:21:50.911
It got through.

00:21:52.496 --> 00:21:53.997
You could really use a shower.

00:21:54.081 --> 00:21:55.165
You, too.